issues.description:
After PI1, run omp-kit test --integrations on every configured profile, enumerated at run time (17 on 2026-10-04: default plus 16 under ~/.omp/profiles, including codex-lean and codex-lean-undo-test created by C6).

The static inventory (rc3/profile-inventory.json) already shows:
- default has the official dcg-guard.ts but no rch or slb bridges;
- 11 named profiles load the local bridges in ~/.omp/omp-extensions (dcg-tool-bridge, rch-mutator, rch-lane-bind-bridge, slb-guard-fail-closed). That directory is not a git repo; the control-plane cp-* beads own those bridges;
- the nv-* profiles have no mcp.json, so no Agent Mail;
- agy, omp-test2 and p15-fake load nothing;
- omp-test loads only kit-guard.

The live run answers whether "configured" means "firing".

Deliver: the matrix in the plan doc, and a bead per real gap. Decide with Josh which profiles are live and which to retire (p15-fake and omp-test2 look like test leftovers).

Josh 2026-10-02: "testing each profile for each integration and reporting what isn't wired in. i'd like to deeply investigate these assumptions".

Why a mock model: a real-model probe (rc3/dcgprobe.sh) showed the codex and claude profiles blocked by dcg-tool-bridge (rules core.git:branch-force-delete, core.filesystem:rm-rf-root-home). The muse model, though, REFUSED to run the commands itself, so dcg was never exercised. A model's choice cannot prove wiring.

Build: for a named profile, copy its agent/config.yml (extensions list with absolute paths), mcp.json and hooks into an isolated HOME (never write the real profile), and add the kit's mock model provider (reuse the scripts/e2e-live.sh mock server and scenario format). Run omp --profile <p> -p against scripted turns. Judge from side effects in scratch, never from model text.

Scenarios, each with a fire case and a quiet near-miss:
- dcg: force-delete a branch in a scratch repo (quiet: list branches);
- slb: a command slb gates (read slb-guard-fail-closed.ts to pick one);
- rch: cargo check in a scratch crate; did the executed input become "rch exec -- ..."? Observe via tool_result or the exec log;
- Agent Mail MCP: a scripted call to health_check (is the server reachable from that profile?);
- kit-guard opt-in: a repo with .omp/kit-guard.json;
- fleet-guard, once shipped: a /tmp write is blocked.

Output: a profile x integration matrix with WIRED / CONFIGURED_NOT_FIRING / ABSENT / LOAD_ERROR, plus evidence paths; exit 0 (it is a report). Static baseline: var/agent-tmp/reality-check.20260930/rc3/profile-inventory.json (produced by profile-inventory.py). Work on main with Agent Mail reservations.

Acceptance: the matrix for muse and codex agrees with the real-model codex result; a planted profile with the dcg extension removed shows ABSENT; nothing writes to ~/.omp.
